<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:vm="using:Phi.Avalonia.Desktop.ViewModels"
             xmlns:views="using:Phi.Avalonia.Desktop.Views"
             xmlns:components="using:Phi.Avalonia.Desktop.Components"
             x:Class="Phi.Avalonia.Desktop.Views.ShellView"
             x:DataType="vm:ShellViewModel">
  <!--
    Two-column shell with a pinned chat chrome on the right side.

    Layout (right column = DockPanel):
      ┌─ Header (DockPanel.Dock=Top, Auto-height) ────────────────┐
      │ Session title                                            │
      ├─ Prompt input (DockPanel.Dock=Bottom, Auto-height) ─────┤
      │ Editor + pickers + send                                  │
      ├─ Transcript (fills remaining space) ──────────────────────┤
      │ ↑ ScrollViewer (its right edge = window right edge) ↑
      │ │  messages                                              │
      │ │  ...                                                  │
      │ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
      └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

    The ScrollViewer is at the DockPanel's MIDDLE (LastChildFill=true),
    so its right edge IS the DockPanel's right edge, which IS the
    right column's right edge, which IS the window's right edge —
    that's where the scrollbar appears. Earlier the ScrollViewer was
    inside ChatPageView (further nested inside the 2*,6*,2* column),
    which clipped it to the 6* reading column's right edge; the
    scrollbar appeared mid-window. Moving the scroll out of the
    chat page and into the shell's pinned chrome structure is what
    makes the scrollbar reach the window edge.

    Header + input are wired via bindings through the dynamic
    <see cref="CurrentPage"/> reference. The bindings evaluate to
    null/default when CurrentPage isn't a ChatPageViewModel (e.g.
    Providers page); the IsVisible flags hide both elements so the
    Providers page renders full-width without the chat chrome.
  -->
  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="280,1,*">
    <views:SidebarView Grid.Column="0" DataContext="{Binding Sidebar}" />
    <GridSplitter Grid.Column="1" Width="1"
                  ResizeDirection="Columns"
                  ResizeBehavior="PreviousAndNext"
                  Background="{DynamicResource ControlStrokeColorDefaultBrush}" />
    <DockPanel Grid.Column="2" LastChildFill="True">

      <!-- Header. Pinned to top via Dock=Top. The border line under
           the header needs to span the full right column width (not
           just the 6* reading column) so the divider visually anchors
           the entire chat surface — the header itself sits at full
           width and is NOT wrapped in 2*,6*,2*. The header Border
           has no 2* margins; the title text inside has Padding for
           its own breathing room. Bound through the casted ChatPage
           property so the XAML compiler resolves HeaderText against
           the concrete ChatPageViewModel type. -->
      <Border DockPanel.Dock="Top"
              IsVisible="{Binding IsChatPage}"
              Padding="20,12,20,12"
              BorderBrush="{DynamicResource SystemControlHighlightBaseMediumLowBrush}"
              BorderThickness="0,0,0,1">
        <TextBlock Text="{Binding ChatPage.HeaderText}"
                   FontSize="14"
                   FontWeight="SemiBold" />
      </Border>

      <!-- Prompt input. Pinned to bottom via Dock=Bottom. Wrapped
           in a 2*,6*,2* Grid so the actual PromptInputView sits in
           the 6* reading column with the same left/right margin as
           the transcript below — without this wrap the input would
           stretch from the right column's left edge to its right
           edge (no breathing room). The outer Grid is the DockPanel
           child (gets the full right column width); the inner column
           structure centres the input. -->
      <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Bottom"
            IsVisible="{Binding IsChatPage}">
        <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>2*,6*,2*</Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
        <ContentControl Grid.Column="1"
                        Content="{Binding ChatPage.PromptInput}">
          <ContentControl.DataTemplates>
            <DataTemplate DataType="vm:PromptInputViewModel">
              <components:PromptInputView />
            </DataTemplate>
          </ContentControl.DataTemplates>
        </ContentControl>
      </Grid>

      <!-- Middle: scrollable transcript. Wraps the routed page
           (ChatPageView or ProvidersPageView). For ChatPage, only the
           ItemsControl renders inside this ScrollViewer — header /
           input are outside in their own DockPanel slots. The scrollbar
           appears at the right edge of this ScrollViewer, which spans
           the entire right column. -->
      <ScrollViewer x:Name="TranscriptScroll"
                    VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                    HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
        <ContentControl Content="{Binding CurrentPage}" />
      </ScrollViewer>

    </DockPanel>
  </Grid>
</UserControl>